               "fundamental":  "Astera Labs\u0027 long-term moat in AI server connectivity is strengthening, not breaking. On Nov 3, 2026, it posted record Q3 revenue of $584.9M (+154% YoY, +49% QoQ), GAAP diluted EPS of $0.99, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.32, beating consensus. Management guided Q4 revenue to $730M–$750M and non-GAAP EPS to $1.62–$1.66, keeping non-GAAP gross margin near 72% after Q3\u0027s 72.4% (non-GAAP operating margin reached 44.7%). Crucially, Scorpio X-Series 320-lane fabric switches scaled into Astera\u0027s largest product family above a $1B annualized run-rate, expanding it beyond PCIe retimers into multi-product rack connectivity alongside Aries 7 (PCIe 7 copper/optical), Leo memory controllers, and the Orion rack architecture partnered with Hyve Solutions. The Nov 20 selloff and Nov 23 surge reflected Nvidia-driven sector shocks and valuation compression rather than business deterioration, though 53% top-customer concentration warrants close monitoring.",
