               "summary":  "Astera Labs (ALAB) surged 23.16% to $222.12 on Nov 23, 2026 as Nvidia\u0027s CEO reinstatement sparked a fierce AI chip rebound, yet shares remain 55.5% below their $499.48 52-week high and beneath all major moving averages. Fundamentally, the moat thesis is intact: Q3 2026 revenue jumped 154% year-over-year to $584.9M on Nov 3 as Scorpio fabric switches surpassed a $1B annualized run-rate, with Q4 revenue guided to $730M–$750M. Still, 53% top-customer concentration, lower GAAP gross margins (72.3%), and steep multiple compression keep volatility extreme.",
               "technical":  "Despite a 23.16% jump to $222.12 on Nov 23, 2026, ALAB\u0027s broader trend remains bearish. Price sits 15%–20% below its EMA 50 ($263.10), EMA 100 ($277.76), and EMA 200 ($260.86) — exponential moving averages tracking medium- and long-term trend direction. Notably, EMA 50 has already slipped below EMA 100 and sits barely above EMA 200, signaling structural weakness; the $260.86–$263.10 band now acts as heavy overhead resistance. On volatility, Bollinger Bands (a 20-day price envelope) span $162.90 to $291.91, reflecting extreme swings. After testing the lower band during the Nov 20 selloff, price rebounded to just under the middle band at $227.41, marking immediate resistance, while $203.65 (Nov 23 low) and $162.90 define key support. ALAB still sits 55.5% below its $499.48 52-week high (low: $97.89). Momentum is stabilizing but not yet bullish: MACD (a trend-momentum gauge) stays deep in negative territory at -21.83, though crossing above its -23.72 signal line (+1.88 histogram), while RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; below 30 is oversold) recovered to 45.77. Volume of 8.47M shares (1.47x the 20-day average of 5.78M) confirmed strong buyer demand on the bounce."
